[readiness/viewer] Verify the static viewer artifact (reviewing)
Files: `viz/index.html` and the viewer contract.
Do: Inspect the viewer at desktop and narrow widths. Exercise corpus selection, primary and comparison views, address focus, group collapse, keyboard selection, metadata and analysis toggles, and clear-focus behavior. Confirm the embedded model remains static and the page makes no network requests or dependency calls. Verify that the viewer presents the addressed architecture substrate and keeps deterministic cost and probabilistic resource overlays separate from structural identity. Decide and record whether the embedded presentation payload is generated from the canonical description through the CLI or remains a curated release snapshot; the canonical description remains the structural source either way. Update only concrete issues found by this check.
Accept: The viewer opens directly without a build step, server, dependency, or network request; the public cases and opaque/deferred states remain inspectable; controls work at desktop and mobile widths; page-level overflow and text overlap are absent; the viewer's relationship to the canonical description is explicit and tested; and no visualization-specific core kind or runtime semantics is introduced.
-> readiness/scope
> The viewer is a read-only presentation over addressed structure, not an architecture authoring surface.
> Address comparison is structural identity; labels, layout, and overlays cannot create or merge elements.
> Cost, placement, measurement, probabilistic resource, and other analysis surfaces remain opt-in views.
> The canonical description remains the only structural source of truth; this release keeps the embedded presentation payload as a curated snapshot assembled from the public case-study fixtures.
> Direct opening is a release requirement; any future generated-payload path must commit or embed presentation data rather than require a server.
> The presentation function is pure with respect to its model and UI state: `renderPresentation(model, uiState)` returns presentation data, while DOM writes and event wiring remain outside it.
---
[readiness/hygiene] Remove publication hazards (reviewing)
Files: `.gitignore` and the tracked-file inventory.
Do: Audit the tracked tree for secrets, generated output, local databases, editor-only state, private paths, and machine-specific caches. Keep intended local outputs ignored and remove unexplained artifacts. Do not add repository configuration that depends on a developer machine or an external checkout.
Accept: The tracked tree contains no generated build output, local database, credential, private path, or unexplained machine-specific artifact; ignore rules cover intended local outputs; and the repository can be checked from a fresh clone.
-> readiness/scope
