[readiness/cost-resources] Implement the cost and resource workflow (reviewing)
Files: the typed resource-flow implementation and existing `crates/grimoire/src/cost.rs`, `crates/grimoire/src/placement.rs`, `crates/grimoire/tests/cost.rs`, `crates/grimoire/tests/placement.rs`, `proposals/cost-layer.md`, `proposals/placement-bandwidth.md`, `proposals/measurement-schema.md`, and the resource-flow contract.
Do: Implement the cost and resource workflow after the resource-flow contract is explicit. Preserve deterministic cost expressions and bytes-on-wire calculations over evaluated addressed structure with caller-supplied axis extents, shapes, placements, and element widths. Add typed resource quantities that can travel, be consumed, transformed, or branch across the addressed graph without treating distinct resource kinds as fungible. Keep observed or estimated values in sourced records with units, protocols, assumptions, and qualified uncertainty. Make missing inputs, invalid probability assumptions, unsupported conversions, and overflow fail visibly; keep analysis values out of structural selection.
Accept: A reader can distinguish exact calculation from probabilistic resource analysis and sourced measurement, follow explicit-input paths, obtain deterministic reports and qualified resource distributions, understand missing-input and invalid-assumption failures, and see that distinct resource kinds remain separate. An indexed-data/search pipeline fixture exercises at least multiple resource kinds and a branch or conditional assumption. No resource result is inferred from names, topology, precision labels, hardware, or runtime behavior.
-> readiness/resource-flow
-> readiness/scope
> Deterministic calculations and probabilistic resource analysis are separate workflows and data accounts.
> Resource kinds are typed and mutually non-interchangeable; no scalar total may add FLOPs, bytes, latency, or memory together.
> Resource flows attach to addressed elements or relations and may be forwarded, consumed, transformed, or split only by explicit rules.
> Probability semantics must distinguish route/workload likelihood from resource-amount variation and measurement uncertainty before implementation chooses a report statistic.
> The existing CostModel and bytes_on_wire APIs remain deterministic analysis surfaces; they do not silently become the probabilistic resource semantics.
> Hardware throughput, device topology, contention, runtime execution, and dtype inference remain outside this workflow.
@artifact text/tsv ./examples/reference-resources.tsv
