[readiness/scry-example] Ground a Scry architecture sample and CLI resource report (reviewing)
Files: `examples/scry.grimoire`, `examples/scry-resources.tsv`, `crates/grimoire/tests/cli.rs`, and `proposals/resource-flow.md`.
Do: Add a public, static Grimoire description of Scry's explicit-origin ingestion, slicing, embedding, persistent corpus, query/search, handle verification, neighbours, provenance, and outer MCP transport boundary. Add sourced measurement records and mutually non-fungible resource scenarios for ingestion and search, with explicit workload probabilities and no inferred hardware behavior. Run the description through the existing CLI commands and compare the resource report with the direct library model in an integration fixture.
Accept: The Scry description validates, canonicalizes, evaluates, and cuts through the CLI; its resource sidecar reports componentwise expected FLOPs, bytes, memory, bandwidth, and latency where authored; scenario assumptions and public source/protocol context are visible; the CLI report agrees with direct `ResourceModel` results; and no Scry dependency, local path, corpus, cache, or MCP configuration enters the tracked Grimoire tree.
-> readiness/cli
-> readiness/resource-flow
> Scry is a public architecture fixture and measurement source, not a Grimoire runtime dependency.
> Scry's MCP server is an outer transport adapter in the sample; it does not become Grimoire's semantic authority.
> Measured quantities and workload probabilities remain explicit analysis inputs; component names and topology do not infer resource values.
